# CHAOS-3742 trial scratch (never commit): .trial-exchange*/ request files
# carry withheld corpus question text verbatim (the file-exchange arm 4/5
# transport writes the real prompt into the request file for the
# out-of-process responder). The trailing `*` matters (sol review F10):
# S3's fresh-session-dir fix creates timestamped dirs like
# .trial-exchange-20260816T125957Z/, which a bare `.trial-exchange/`
# pattern does NOT match. .probe-tmp/ is throwaway runner scripts/logs.
.trial-exchange*/
.probe-tmp/

# codex-review SKILL scratch files (.claude/skills/codex-review/SKILL.md):
# a lane's per-worktree `git/info/exclude` keeps these out of `git status`
# during review, but that file is per-clone, not committed -- this repo-wide
# .gitignore entry is the backstop so a squash-merge can't accidentally
# carry one in again (codex-gate-r2.log/.md landed on main via #335's squash).
prompt.md
.codex-review-context.md
LEDGER.md
codex-gate.md
codex-gate.log
codex-gate-*.md
codex-gate-*.log

# Go build cache written INTO the worktree by a sandboxed tool run (a
# read-only codex review redirects GOCACHE here rather than to the user
# cache). 284 MB / 2700+ files, host-specific and never source. Ignored
# because `git add -A` swept it into a commit once and only an adversarial
# review caught it.
.gocache/
